"comments": {
"@0btgq037t1l2mfm323ppoj6ntg": "A style element holding these rules.",
"@0l1rjlto5fkijtkda86k2hcn1g": "A div with these children. To give it attributes, wrap it: styled, classed, with.",
"@12vme77vlgm2ldkqg243hvdh9o": "The same element with these attributes added after its own. Text and parts have no attributes, so they come back as they are.",
"@53pjvtvb581kaggvi0cceir9q1": "A ul element with these children: a list with bullets, whose items are li.",
"@64ufrjcboejfrlftcbbdgmf07o": "A p element with these children: a paragraph.",
"@8sehpubpftejqnj9slepmavak6": "A strong element with these children: important text, usually bold.",
"@8tin5pqh5scbr0ebk350tklhe4": "A label element with these children: a label for a field.",
"@a8e1ijgplu67sqsl5boqvo1ma7": "A h2 element with these children: a second-level heading.",
"@cg4a2dcbo8fm06hjv7c8ak01ao": "The items of a cell's list, each drawn by row and all put inside (ul, div, …). An item still there when the list changes keeps its row as it was; only new items get one. Solid's <For> (prior art).",
"@d2d31mg504n8hk8h2mntf0acis": "Text that doesn't change. Text that does is text(() => …), which the page runs again when what it reads changes.",
"@dogubk0ef9veunk39t9c98amip": "An input field: it has attributes and no children.",
"@h5sld79ct1qljlaaltbt7hlegi": "A section element with these children: a part of the page.",
"@jka8f1t2ulg3auovstbcohk8u7": "The same element with this id.",
"@l1ibnd69fhv5j8j3reredg1ar1": "A style sheet rule: a selector and its declarations. A style sheet is a list of these, so it shows rule by rule instead of as one long text.",
"@luti73h3nrj77st364r0mm7s5c": "A h1 element with these children: the biggest heading.",
"@mpfopvrjbtvkmsfp87511ienno": "A li element with these children: one item of a list.",
"@n3tuqn9rsv5veg67i1ug2od394": "An element with these children, for a tag that has no function of its own here (main, nav, table, …). Each tag a function, as in Elm's Html module (prior art).",
"@o7uhehv54sp47usn1r5ujam1vk": "The same element with this inline style (CSS declarations, such as color: #777; margin: 0).",
"@oltnlntd2q3g3n7avkcoddufbh": "A button with this label that runs then when it's clicked.",
"@r6va5gq576cc5qk3t5nvk5a046": "The same element in this class, for a style sheet's rules to select.",
"@rrc61bud51hgr319omhcik166b": "The texts with between between each two of them.",
"@sse8s4j5eo5cs94stokicn369f": "A span element with these children: a run of text inside a line.",
"@unasag7492jo4l95p7s018eeji": "A footer element with these children: the page's foot.",
"@urmvgd3e2dcctt7q85g15nql15": "Rules that apply only when the query holds, such as (prefers-color-scheme: dark).",
"@v4m3u10hkehjb5097mejohqi5p": "A length in pixels, from a Float64 or an Int.",
"@verpptg1dl3oqd6ba55ri1mcah": "An attribute whose value doesn't change."
},
